    "name": "Mini-Cycle",
    "text": "2\nMini-Cycle\n1 SECTION\nInstructions\n\nNOTE: Mini-Cycles involve working through full LR sections in batches of 9 questions at a time, without breaks between batches. Do not do less than a full section*.\n\nFor questions #1-3, translate and CLIR the stimulus only.\n\nDo not look at the question stem or answer choices yet.\n\nFor questions #4-6, Party Trick the answer choices only.\n\nDo not read the stimulus yet.\n\nFor questions #7-9, complete the full question according to the straight-through LR Full Question Process.\n\nReturn to questions #1-3 and Party Trick them.\n\nAfter Party Tricking #1-3, relook at the stimulus and change your answer if needed.\n\nReturn to questions #4-6 and translate and CLIR.\n\nChoose an answer based on your new understanding of the stimulus.\n\nNote if the answer choice differs from your original Party-Tricked choice.\n\nRepeat this process with the next 9 questions, and then again with the remaining questions in the section. It’s expected that the last batch of questions is less than 9, so you won’t do as many full questions in that batch.\n\nSEE FULL WORKOUT DETAILS",
